    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="0751" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg739"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/9–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Appointed Minister to Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-12T17:00:00-04:00">September 12,
                            1944—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>177. ReLegs 270, September 8, 2 p.m. Department and FEA approve of agreement
                    reached in Jidda, set forth in paragraph (B) of Cairo’s 2687, September 8, 6
                        p.m.,<anchor n="52" xml:id="d807-f1"/> to increase grain shipments from
                    40,000 to 50,000 tons under joint American-British supply program for Saudi
                    Arabia during 1944. Department and FEA also approve of use of 50,000 ton figure
                    as provisional basis in determining amount of grain to be supplied during
                    1945.</p>
                <p>You and your British colleague jointly should notify King Ibn Saud of the
                    10,000-ton increase in grain supplies under the 1944 program as soon as your
                    British colleague receives similar instructions from his Government.</p>
                <p>Sent to Jidda, repeated to Cairo<anchor n="53" xml:id="d807-f2"/> for AEMME.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d807-f1" n="52" xml:id="d807-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; paragraph B repeated terms of agreement for supply as described by
                    the Appointed Minister to Saudi Arabia in his telegram 270, September 8. 2 p.m.,
                        <ref target="#pg736">p. 736</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d807-f2" n="53" xml:id="d807-f2-content">
                <p>Repeated to Cairo as telegram 2457.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
